        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(qa-lab): runtime parity stays bounded when mock debug snapshots are oversized",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where QA runtime parity reports could stall or consume unbounded memory when a mock provider debug snapshot grows unexpectedly large.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe QA-lab runtime parity mock `/debug/requests` capture now uses the existing plugin SDK bounded response reader with a 1 MiB cap. Overflow and malformed debug payloads keep the existing best-effort `null` result so transcript-derived tool-call fallback remains the recovery path.\n\n## User Impact\n\nQA runtime parity runs stay responsive when local mock debug payloads are oversized, while normal debug snapshots continue to contribute tool-call ordering details.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: oversized mock debug snapshots are bounded, the debug response is cancelled, and runtime parity falls back to transcript-derived final text and tool calls.\n- Real behavior proof at 5d0d3143362021d8eeaeffcd8942e800ed3f5f14: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/qa-lab/src/runtime-parity.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/runtime-parity.capture.test.ts` passed with 2 test files and 9 tests. The capture test starts a real localhost `/debug/requests` HTTP endpoint that does not end on its own, calls `captureRuntimeParityCell` with that `mockBaseUrl`, and verifies the cell returns transcript-derived `done` text plus the `read_file` tool call after the response closes.\n- Redacted terminal summary from the real-path proof: `Test Files 2 passed (2)`, `Tests 9 passed (9)`, `[test] passed 1 Vitest shard in 39.80s`.\n- PR diff hygiene: `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD` passed.\n- Review proof: `python .agents\\skills\\autoreview\\scripts\\autoreview --mode branch --base upstream/main` passed with no accepted/actionable findings.",
